      "notes": "\n  <h2>Gases</h2>\n\n  <p>A gas is a state of matter in which particles are far apart and move\n  freely in all directions.</p>\n\n  <h3>Particle Arrangement</h3>\n\n  <p>Gas particles are widely separated with large amounts of empty space\n  between them.</p>\n\n  <h3>Particle Movement</h3>\n\n  <p>The particles move rapidly and randomly in all directions.</p>\n\n  <h3>Properties of Gases</h3>\n\n  <ul>\n    <li>They have no fixed shape.</li>\n    <li>They have no fixed volume.</li>\n    <li>They fill their containers.</li>\n    <li>They are easily compressed.</li>\n    <li>They can flow.</li>\n    <li>They exert pressure on the walls of their containers.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h3>Examples</h3>\n\n  <p>Oxygen, nitrogen, carbon dioxide and water vapour are examples of gases\n  under suitable conditions.</p>\n  ",
