      "notes": "<h2>Homogeneous Mixtures</h2>\n\n  <p>A <strong>homogeneous mixture</strong> is a mixture whose composition is uniform throughout.</p>\n\n  <p>Every part of the mixture has essentially the same composition and properties.</p>\n\n  <h3>Examples</h3>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Salt solution</li>\n    <li>Sugar solution</li>\n    <li>Air</li>\n    <li>Brass</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h3>Key features</h3>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Uniform composition throughout.</li>\n    <li>Components are not normally visibly distinguishable.</li>\n    <li>It is still a mixture.</li>\n    <li>Its components can be separated by suitable physical methods.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h3>Example</h3>\n  <p>When salt dissolves completely in water, the salt particles become evenly distributed throughout the water. A sample taken from the top has the same composition as a sample taken from the bottom, assuming the solution is properly mixed.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>Homogeneous = uniform throughout.</strong></p>",
