      "notes": "<h2>Heterogeneous Mixtures</h2>\n\n  <p>A <strong>heterogeneous mixture</strong> is a mixture whose composition is not uniform throughout.</p>\n\n  <p>Different parts of the mixture may contain different amounts or types of components.</p>\n\n  <h3>Examples</h3>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Sand and water</li>\n    <li>Oil and water</li>\n    <li>Iron filings and sulfur</li>\n    <li>Sand and gravel</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h3>Key features</h3>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Composition is not uniform.</li>\n    <li>Different components may be visibly distinguishable.</li>\n    <li>Different portions can have different compositions.</li>\n    <li>Components can usually be separated using physical methods.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h3>Example</h3>\n  <p>In a mixture of sand and water, the sand settles at the bottom while water remains above it. The composition is therefore not uniform throughout the sample.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>Heterogeneous = non-uniform throughout.</strong></p>",
