      "notes": "<h2>Magnetic Separation</h2>\n\n  <p><strong>Magnetic separation</strong> is used when one component of a mixture is attracted to a magnet while the other component is not.</p>\n\n  <h3>Principle</h3>\n  <p>The method depends on a difference in <strong>magnetic properties</strong>.</p>\n\n  <h3>Procedure</h3>\n  <ol>\n    <li>Bring a magnet close to the mixture.</li>\n    <li>The magnetic component is attracted to the magnet.</li>\n    <li>The non-magnetic component remains behind.</li>\n    <li>Remove the magnetic material from the magnet.</li>\n  </ol>\n\n  <h3>Example</h3>\n  <p>Iron filings can be separated from sulfur powder using a magnet.</p>\n\n  <h3>Important point</h3>\n  <p>The method only works when the components have sufficiently different magnetic properties.</p>",
