      "notes": "<h2>Protons</h2>\n\n  <p>A <strong>proton</strong> is a positively charged subatomic particle found in the nucleus of an atom.</p>\n\n  <ul>\n    <li>Relative charge = <strong>+1</strong></li>\n    <li>Relative mass ≈ <strong>1</strong></li>\n    <li>Location = <strong>nucleus</strong></li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p>The number of protons determines the identity of an element.</p>\n\n  <p>For example:</p>\n\n  <ul>\n    <li>Hydrogen has 1 proton.</li>\n    <li>Carbon has 6 protons.</li>\n    <li>Oxygen has 8 protons.</li>\n    <li>Sodium has 11 protons.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p><strong>Change the number of protons → change the element.</strong></p>",
