      "notes": "<h2>Atomic Number</h2>\n\n  <p>The <strong>atomic number</strong> of an element is the number of protons in the nucleus of its atoms.</p>\n\n  <p>It is represented by <strong>Z</strong>.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>Atomic number = number of protons</strong></p>\n\n  <p>For a neutral atom:</p>\n\n  <p><strong>Atomic number = number of protons = number of electrons</strong></p>\n\n  <h3>Examples</h3>\n\n  <ul>\n    <li>Hydrogen: Z = 1</li>\n    <li>Carbon: Z = 6</li>\n    <li>Oxygen: Z = 8</li>\n    <li>Sodium: Z = 11</li>\n    <li>Chlorine: Z = 17</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p>The atomic number identifies the element.</p>",
