      "notes": "<h2>Mass Number</h2>\n\n  <p>The <strong>mass number</strong> is the total number of protons and neutrons in the nucleus of an atom.</p>\n\n  <p>It is represented by <strong>A</strong>.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>Mass number = protons + neutrons</strong></p>\n\n  <p>Therefore:</p>\n\n  <p><strong>Neutrons = mass number − protons</strong></p>\n\n  <h3>Example</h3>\n\n  <p>An atom has 11 protons and 12 neutrons:</p>\n\n  <p>Mass number = 11 + 12 = <strong>23</strong></p>\n\n  <p>Electrons are not included in the mass number because their mass is extremely small compared with that of protons and neutrons.</p>",
