      "notes": "<h2>Isotopes</h2>\n\n  <p><strong>Isotopes</strong> are atoms of the same element that have the same number of protons but different numbers of neutrons.</p>\n\n  <h3>What remains the same?</h3>\n\n  <p>Isotopes of an element have the same:</p>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Number of protons</li>\n    <li>Atomic number</li>\n    <li>Element identity</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h3>What changes?</h3>\n\n  <p>They have different:</p>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Numbers of neutrons</li>\n    <li>Mass numbers</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h3>Example: carbon</h3>\n\n  <p>Carbon-12:</p>\n  <p>6 protons + 6 neutrons = 12</p>\n\n  <p>Carbon-14:</p>\n  <p>6 protons + 8 neutrons = 14</p>\n\n  <p>Both are carbon because both contain 6 protons.</p>",
