      "notes": "<h2>Group 1 Elements</h2>\n\n  <p>Group 1 elements are called the <strong>alkali metals</strong>.</p>\n\n  <h3>Examples</h3>\n\n  <ul>\n    <li>Lithium — Li</li>\n    <li>Sodium — Na</li>\n    <li>Potassium — K</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h3>Electron arrangement</h3>\n\n  <p>Group 1 elements have <strong>one electron in their outermost energy level</strong>.</p>\n\n  <p>Examples:</p>\n\n  <ul>\n    <li>Li = 2,1</li>\n    <li>Na = 2,8,1</li>\n    <li>K = 2,8,8,1</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h3>Reaction with water</h3>\n\n  <p>Group 1 metals react with water to form a metal hydroxide and hydrogen gas.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>metal + water → metal hydroxide + hydrogen</strong></p>\n\n  <p>The metals generally become more reactive down the group.</p>",
