      "notes": "<h2>Group 2 Elements</h2>\n\n  <p>Group 2 elements are called the <strong>alkaline earth metals</strong>.</p>\n\n  <h3>Examples</h3>\n\n  <ul>\n    <li>Beryllium — Be</li>\n    <li>Magnesium — Mg</li>\n    <li>Calcium — Ca</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h3>Electron arrangement</h3>\n\n  <p>Group 2 elements have <strong>two electrons in their outermost energy level</strong>.</p>\n\n  <p>Examples:</p>\n\n  <ul>\n    <li>Be = 2,2</li>\n    <li>Mg = 2,8,2</li>\n    <li>Ca = 2,8,8,2</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p>They commonly lose two electrons to form <strong>2+</strong> ions.</p>\n\n  <h3>Reaction with water</h3>\n\n  <p>Some Group 2 metals react with water to form metal hydroxides and hydrogen. Reactivity generally increases down the group.</p>",
