      "notes": "<h2>Group 7 Elements</h2>\n\n  <p>Group 7 elements are called the <strong>halogens</strong>.</p>\n\n  <h3>Examples</h3>\n\n  <ul>\n    <li>Fluorine — F</li>\n    <li>Chlorine — Cl</li>\n    <li>Bromine — Br</li>\n    <li>Iodine — I</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p>For the first 20 elements, fluorine and chlorine are important examples.</p>\n\n  <h3>Electron arrangement</h3>\n\n  <p>Group 7 elements have <strong>seven outer electrons</strong>.</p>\n\n  <p>Example:</p>\n\n  <p>Chlorine = 2,8,7</p>\n\n  <p>They tend to gain one electron to obtain a stable outer shell, forming <strong>1− ions</strong>.</p>\n\n  <h3>Reactivity</h3>\n\n  <p>Halogen reactivity generally decreases down the group.</p>",
