      "notes": "<h2>Group 0 Elements</h2>\n\n  <p>Group 0 elements are called the <strong>noble gases</strong>.</p>\n\n  <h3>Examples</h3>\n\n  <ul>\n    <li>Helium — He</li>\n    <li>Neon — Ne</li>\n    <li>Argon — Ar</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h3>Electron arrangement</h3>\n\n  <p>Noble gases have full outer energy levels.</p>\n\n  <ul>\n    <li>Helium = 2</li>\n    <li>Neon = 2,8</li>\n    <li>Argon = 2,8,8</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p>Because their outer energy levels are full, noble gases are generally very unreactive.</p>\n\n  <h3>Physical state</h3>\n\n  <p>At room temperature, noble gases are gases.</p>",
