      "notes": "<h2>Formation of Negative Ions</h2>\n\n  <p>A <strong>negative ion</strong>, or <strong>anion</strong>, forms when an atom gains one or more electrons.</p>\n\n  <p>Because electrons have negative charges, gaining electrons gives the atom an overall negative charge.</p>\n\n  <h3>Chlorine</h3>\n\n  <p>Cl = 2,8,7</p>\n\n  <p>Cl + e⁻ → Cl⁻</p>\n\n  <p>Chlorine gains one electron and becomes Cl⁻.</p>\n\n  <h3>Oxygen</h3>\n\n  <p>O = 2,6</p>\n\n  <p>O + 2e⁻ → O²⁻</p>\n\n  <p>Oxygen gains two electrons and becomes O²⁻.</p>",
