      "notes": "<h2>Covalent Bonding</h2>\n\n  <p><strong>Covalent bonding</strong> occurs when atoms share pairs of electrons.</p>\n\n  <p>Covalent bonding commonly occurs between non-metal atoms.</p>\n\n  <h3>Why electrons are shared</h3>\n\n  <p>Sharing electrons allows the bonded atoms to obtain more stable outer-electron arrangements.</p>\n\n  <h3>Hydrogen molecule</h3>\n\n  <p>Each hydrogen atom has one electron.</p>\n\n  <p>Each hydrogen atom needs one more electron to fill its first energy level.</p>\n\n  <p>The two hydrogen atoms share one pair of electrons.</p>\n\n  <p>H—H</p>\n\n  <p>The shared pair forms a <strong>single covalent bond</strong>.</p>",
