      "notes": "<h2>Giant Covalent Structures</h2>\n\n  <p>A <strong>giant covalent structure</strong> contains a very large number of atoms joined together by covalent bonds in a continuous structure.</p>\n\n  <p>Unlike simple molecular substances, giant covalent substances do not consist of separate small molecules.</p>\n\n  <h3>Examples</h3>\n\n  <ul>\n    <li>Diamond</li>\n    <li>Graphite</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h3>General properties</h3>\n\n  <ul>\n    <li>Strong covalent bonds extend throughout the structure.</li>\n    <li>Large amounts of energy are required to break these bonds.</li>\n    <li>They generally have very high melting points.</li>\n  </ul>",
