      "notes": "<h2>Diamond</h2>\n\n  <p><strong>Diamond</strong> is a giant covalent form of carbon.</p>\n\n  <h3>Structure</h3>\n\n  <p>Each carbon atom is covalently bonded to four other carbon atoms.</p>\n\n  <p>This forms a strong three-dimensional giant structure.</p>\n\n  <h3>Properties</h3>\n\n  <ul>\n    <li>Very hard.</li>\n    <li>Very high melting point.</li>\n    <li>Does not conduct electricity.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h3>Why diamond is hard</h3>\n\n  <p>Strong covalent bonds extend throughout the three-dimensional structure, making it difficult to move one carbon atom past another.</p>\n\n  <h3>Why diamond does not conduct electricity</h3>\n\n  <p>All the outer electrons of carbon are involved in covalent bonds, so there are no freely mobile electrons available to carry electric charge.</p>",
