          "why": "The number of particles is proportional to the number of moles.",
          "sol": "Step 1: Use N = nNₐ.\nStep 2: n = 2 mol.\nStep 3: Nₐ = 6.02 × 10²³ mol⁻¹.\nStep 4: N = 2 × 6.02 × 10²³.\nStep 5: N = 12.04 × 10²³.\nStep 6: N = 1.204 × 10²⁴ particles.",
          "hint": "Focus on the core principle of Avogadro Constant.",
          "subject": "chemistry",
