      "notes": "<h2>Molar Mass</h2>\n\n  <p><strong>Molar mass</strong> is the mass of one mole of a substance.</p>\n\n  <p>It is measured in <strong>g mol⁻¹</strong>.</p>\n\n  <p>The numerical value of molar mass corresponds to the relative atomic mass or relative formula mass.</p>\n\n  <h3>Examples</h3>\n\n  <p>H₂O:</p>\n\n  <p>Mᵣ = 18</p>\n\n  <p>Therefore molar mass = <strong>18 g mol⁻¹</strong>.</p>\n\n  <p>CO₂:</p>\n\n  <p>Mᵣ = 44</p>\n\n  <p>Therefore molar mass = <strong>44 g mol⁻¹</strong>.</p>",
