          "steps": [
            "Step 1: Use n = m ÷ M.",
            "Step 2: m = 36 g.",
            "Step 3: M = 18 g mol⁻¹.",
            "Step 4: n = 36 ÷ 18.",
            "Step 5: n = 2 mol."
          ],
          "why": "The mass is divided by the mass of one mole.",
          "sol": "Step 1: Use n = m ÷ M.\nStep 2: m = 36 g.\nStep 3: M = 18 g mol⁻¹.\nStep 4: n = 36 ÷ 18.\nStep 5: n = 2 mol.",
          "hint": "Focus on the core principle of Calculating Moles from Mass.",
          "subject": "chemistry",
