      "notes": "<h2>Moles and Particles</h2>\n\n  <p>Moles and number of particles are directly related through the Avogadro constant.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>N = nNₐ</strong></p>\n\n  <p>Therefore:</p>\n\n  <p><strong>particles = moles × 6.02 × 10²³</strong></p>\n\n  <p>And:</p>\n\n  <p><strong>moles = particles ÷ 6.02 × 10²³</strong></p>\n\n  <h3>Important</h3>\n\n  <p>Always identify what type of particle is being counted: atoms, molecules or ions.</p>",
