          "steps": [
            "Step 1: Fe₂O₃ contains 2 Fe atoms and 3 O atoms.",
            "Step 2: Use 2Fe₂O₃ to give 4 Fe atoms and 6 O atoms.",
            "Step 3: Put 4 before Fe.",
            "Step 4: Put 3 before O₂ to give 6 oxygen atoms.",
            "Step 5: Check both elements."
          ],
          "why": "There are 4 iron atoms and 6 oxygen atoms on each side.",
          "sol": "Step 1: Fe₂O₃ contains 2 Fe atoms and 3 O atoms.\nStep 2: Use 2Fe₂O₃ to give 4 Fe atoms and 6 O atoms.\nStep 3: Put 4 before Fe.\nStep 4: Put 3 before O₂ to give 6 oxygen atoms.\nStep 5: Check both elements.",
          "hint": "Focus on the core principle of Balancing More Complex Equations.",
          "subject": "chemistry",
          "chapter": "chemical_reactions",
          "topic": "Balancing More Complex Equations",
          "conceptId": "chemistry_chemical_reactions_balancing_more_complex_equations",
          "skillId": "chemistry_chemical_reactions",
          "subskillId": "chemistry_chemical_reactions_q1"
