      "notes": "<h2>Reactions of Acids with Metals</h2>\n  <p>Dilute acids react with suitable metals to form a <strong>salt and hydrogen gas</strong>.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>Acid + Metal → Salt + Hydrogen</strong></p>\n\n  <h3>Example</h3>\n  <p>Magnesium reacts with hydrochloric acid:</p>\n  <p><strong>Mg + 2HCl → MgCl<sub>2</sub> + H<sub>2</sub></strong></p>\n\n  <p>Fizzing occurs because hydrogen gas is produced.</p>",
