      "notes": "<h2>Bases</h2>\n  <p>A base is a substance that reacts with an acid to form a salt and water.</p>\n\n  <p>Many metal oxides and metal hydroxides are bases.</p>\n\n  <p>Examples include:</p>\n  <ul>\n    <li>CuO — copper(II) oxide</li>\n    <li>MgO — magnesium oxide</li>\n    <li>Cu(OH)<sub>2</sub> — copper(II) hydroxide</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p>Some bases are soluble in water. These soluble bases are called <strong>alkalis</strong>.</p>",
