      "notes": "<h2>pH Scale</h2>\n  <p>The pH scale is used to describe how acidic or alkaline an aqueous solution is.</p>\n\n  <p>The commonly used scale runs from about <strong>0 to 14</strong>.</p>\n\n  <ul>\n    <li>pH below 7 = acidic</li>\n    <li>pH 7 = neutral</li>\n    <li>pH above 7 = alkaline</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p>The lower the pH, the more acidic the solution generally is.</p>\n  <p>The higher the pH, the more alkaline the solution generally is.</p>",
