          "why": "This prevents unreacted acid from remaining in the salt solution.",
          "sol": "Step 1: The carbonate is added to the acid.\nStep 2: Excess carbonate ensures that all the acid reacts.\nStep 3: The remaining solid carbonate can be removed by filtration.",
          "hint": "Focus on the core principle of Preparing Soluble Salts from Acids and Carbonates.",
          "subject": "chemistry",
          "chapter": "acids_bases_salts",
