      "notes": "<h2>Endothermic Reactions</h2>\n  <p>An endothermic reaction is a chemical reaction that absorbs energy from the surroundings.</p>\n\n  <p>The absorbed energy is often transferred as heat, causing the surroundings to become cooler.</p>\n\n  <h3>Examples</h3>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Thermal decomposition of calcium carbonate</li>\n    <li>Some reactions between salts and water</li>\n    <li>Photosynthesis</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p>For an endothermic reaction, energy is transferred from the surroundings into the reacting system.</p>",
