      "notes": "<h2>Rate of Reaction</h2>\n  <p>The rate of a chemical reaction describes how quickly reactants are used up or products are formed.</p>\n\n  <p>A reaction that happens quickly has a high rate. A reaction that happens slowly has a low rate.</p>\n\n  <h3>Simple expression</h3>\n  <p><strong>Rate = change in amount ÷ time taken</strong></p>\n\n  <p>The amount may be measured using mass, volume, concentration or another suitable quantity.</p>",
