          "why": "Iron(III) oxide loses oxygen to form iron.",
          "sol": "Step 1: Compare the reactant and product containing iron.\nStep 2: Fe₂O₃ changes into Fe.\nStep 3: Oxygen has been removed from the iron compound.",
          "hint": "Focus on the core principle of Reduction.",
          "subject": "chemistry",
          "chapter": "metals_extraction",
          "topic": "Reduction",
          "conceptId": "chemistry_metals_extraction_reduction",
