      "notes": "<h2>Electroplating</h2>\n\n  <p><strong>Electroplating</strong> is the coating of one metal object with a thin layer of another metal using electrolysis.</p>\n\n  <h3>Arrangement</h3>\n\n  <ul>\n    <li>The object to be coated is made the <strong>cathode</strong>.</li>\n    <li>The coating metal is usually the <strong>anode</strong>.</li>\n    <li>The electrolyte contains ions of the coating metal.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p>For copper plating, Cu²⁺ ions gain electrons at the object:</p>\n\n  <p><strong>Cu²⁺ + 2e⁻ → Cu</strong></p>\n\n  <p>Copper is therefore deposited onto the cathode.</p>",
