      "notes": "<h2>Applications of Electrolysis</h2>\n\n  <p>Electrolysis has several important applications.</p>\n\n  <ul>\n    <li>Extraction of very reactive metals.</li>\n    <li>Electroplating objects.</li>\n    <li>Purification of metals.</li>\n    <li>Manufacture of useful chemicals.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h3>Examples</h3>\n\n  <p><strong>Extraction:</strong> Aluminium is extracted from molten aluminium oxide by electrolysis because aluminium is too reactive to be extracted by ordinary chemical reduction with carbon.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>Electroplating:</strong> Objects can be coated with metals such as copper, nickel or chromium.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>Purification:</strong> Electrolysis can be used to purify copper.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>Chemical manufacture:</strong> Electrolysis of brine is used industrially to produce chlorine, hydrogen and sodium hydroxide.</p>",
