      "notes": "<h2>Catenation</h2>\n\n  <p><strong>Catenation</strong> is the ability of an element to form covalent bonds with atoms of the same element, producing chains, branches or rings.</p>\n\n  <p>Carbon shows extensive catenation.</p>\n\n  <p>Carbon atoms can join together to form:</p>\n\n  <ul>\n    <li>Short chains</li>\n    <li>Long chains</li>\n    <li>Branched chains</li>\n    <li>Rings</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h3>Examples</h3>\n\n  <p>Methane: CH₄ → one carbon atom.</p>\n\n  <p>Ethane: C₂H₆ → two carbon atoms joined together.</p>\n\n  <p>Propane: C₃H₈ → three carbon atoms joined in a chain.</p>\n\n  <p>Butane: C₄H₁₀ → four carbon atoms joined in a chain.</p>",
