      "notes": "<h2>Alkanes</h2>\n\n  <p><strong>Alkanes</strong> are saturated hydrocarbons containing only carbon-carbon single bonds.</p>\n\n  <p>The general formula for open-chain alkanes is:</p>\n\n  <p><strong>CₙH₂ₙ₊₂</strong></p>\n\n  <h3>First members</h3>\n\n  <ul>\n    <li>Methane — CH₄</li>\n    <li>Ethane — C₂H₆</li>\n    <li>Propane — C₃H₈</li>\n    <li>Butane — C₄H₁₀</li>\n    <li>Pentane — C₅H₁₂</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h3>Example</h3>\n\n  <p>For n = 4:</p>\n\n  <p>H = 2(4) + 2 = 10</p>\n\n  <p>Therefore the formula is C₄H₁₀.</p>",
