      "notes": "<h2>Homologous Series</h2>\n\n  <p>A <strong>homologous series</strong> is a family of organic compounds with:</p>\n\n  <ul>\n    <li>The same functional group.</li>\n    <li>The same general formula.</li>\n    <li>Similar chemical properties.</li>\n    <li>A gradual change in physical properties.</li>\n    <li>Successive members differing by a <strong>CH₂</strong> unit.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h3>Example: Alkanes</h3>\n\n  <p>Methane: CH₄</p>\n\n  <p>Ethane: C₂H₆</p>\n\n  <p>Propane: C₃H₈</p>\n\n  <p>Butane: C₄H₁₀</p>\n\n  <p>Each successive member differs from the previous one by CH₂.</p>",
