      "notes": "<h2>Naming Alkynes</h2>\n\n  <p>Alkynes contain at least one carbon-carbon triple bond.</p>\n\n  <p>The suffix used for alkynes is <strong>-yne</strong>.</p>\n\n  <h3>Rules</h3>\n\n  <p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Find the longest carbon chain containing the triple bond.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Number the chain from the end nearest to the triple bond.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Identify the position where the triple bond begins.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>Step 4:</strong> Use the carbon prefix and the ending <strong>-yne</strong>.</p>\n\n  <h3>Examples</h3>\n\n  <p>HC≡CH → ethyne</p>\n\n  <p>CH≡C–CH₃ → propyne</p>\n\n  <p>CH≡C–CH₂–CH₃ → but-1-yne</p>\n\n  <p>CH₃–C≡C–CH₃ → but-2-yne</p>",
