          "why": "The two forms differ only in the spatial arrangement around the carbon-carbon double bond.",
          "sol": "Step 1: Both compounds have the same molecular formula, C₄H₈.\nStep 2: Both have the same carbon-carbon connectivity.\nStep 3: In cis-but-2-ene, the similar groups are on the same side of the double bond.\nStep 4: In trans-but-2-ene, the similar groups are on opposite sides.",
          "hint": "Focus on the core principle of Geometric Isomerism.",
          "subject": "chemistry",
          "chapter": "organic_chemistry",
          "topic": "Geometric Isomerism",
          "conceptId": "chemistry_organic_chemistry_geometric_isomerism",
          "skillId": "chemistry_organic_chemistry",
          "subskillId": "chemistry_organic_chemistry_q2"
