      "notes": "<h2>Ethanol</h2>\n\n  <p>Ethanol is a two-carbon alcohol.</p>\n\n  <p>Its molecular formula is:</p>\n\n  <p><strong>C₂H₆O</strong></p>\n\n  <p>It is commonly written as:</p>\n\n  <p><strong>C₂H₅OH</strong></p>\n\n  <p>Its structural formula is:</p>\n\n  <p><strong>CH₃CH₂OH</strong></p>\n\n  <h3>Structure</h3>\n\n  <p>Ethanol contains:</p>\n\n  <ul>\n    <li>2 carbon atoms</li>\n    <li>6 hydrogen atoms</li>\n    <li>1 oxygen atom</li>\n    <li>1 hydroxyl group, –OH</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p>The two-carbon chain gives the prefix <strong>eth-</strong>, while the –OH functional group identifies it as an alcohol.</p>",
