      "notes": "<h2>Oxidation of Ethanol</h2>\n\n  <p>Ethanol can be oxidised to form <strong>ethanoic acid</strong>.</p>\n\n  <p>This can occur when ethanol is exposed to oxygen in the presence of suitable microorganisms, or when an oxidising agent is used in the laboratory.</p>\n\n  <h3>Overall change</h3>\n\n  <p><strong>Ethanol → ethanoic acid</strong></p>\n\n  <p>In the presence of oxygen:</p>\n\n  <p><strong>C₂H₅OH + O₂ → CH₃COOH + H₂O</strong></p>\n\n  <h3>Observation</h3>\n\n  <p>The reaction changes the alcohol into a carboxylic acid.</p>\n\n  <p>Oxidation therefore provides an important link between alcohols and carboxylic acids.</p>",
