      "notes": "<h2>Reactions of Ethanoic Acid</h2>\n\n  <p>Ethanoic acid shows the typical reactions of an acid.</p>\n\n  <h3>1. Reaction with reactive metals</h3>\n\n  <p>Ethanoic acid reacts with some reactive metals to produce a salt and hydrogen gas.</p>\n\n  <p>For example:</p>\n\n  <p><strong>2CH₃COOH + Mg → (CH₃COO)₂Mg + H₂</strong></p>\n\n  <h3>2. Reaction with carbonates</h3>\n\n  <p>Ethanoic acid reacts with carbonates to produce a salt, water and carbon dioxide.</p>\n\n  <p>For example:</p>\n\n  <p><strong>2CH₃COOH + Na₂CO₃ → 2CH₃COONa + H₂O + CO₂</strong></p>\n\n  <h3>3. Reaction with alkalis</h3>\n\n  <p>Ethanoic acid reacts with an alkali in a neutralisation reaction.</p>\n\n  <p>For example:</p>\n\n  <p><strong>CH₃COOH + NaOH → CH₃COONa + H₂O</strong></p>\n\n  <p>The salt formed with sodium hydroxide is sodium ethanoate.</p>",
