      "notes": "<h2>Properties of Oxygen</h2>\n\n  <p>Oxygen is a colourless, odourless and tasteless gas at room temperature.</p>\n\n  <ul>\n    <li>It is slightly soluble in water.</li>\n    <li>It is slightly denser than air.</li>\n    <li>It does not burn itself.</li>\n    <li>It supports combustion.</li>\n    <li>It is essential for respiration.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h3>Test for oxygen</h3>\n  <p>A glowing splint is inserted into the gas. If the splint relights, oxygen is present.</p>\n\n  <h3>Combustion</h3>\n  <p>Carbon burns in oxygen:</p>\n\n  <p><strong>C + O₂ → CO₂</strong></p>",
