          "why": "Each water molecule contains two hydrogen atoms and one oxygen atom.",
          "sol": "Step 1: Water contains hydrogen and oxygen.\nStep 2: Two hydrogen atoms combine with one oxygen atom.\nStep 3: Therefore, the formula is H₂O.",
          "hint": "Focus on the core principle of Properties of Water.",
          "subject": "chemistry",
