          "ans": "Calcium and magnesium ions react with soap to form insoluble scum.",
          "type": "text",
          "options": [],
          "steps": [
            "Step 1: Hard water contains Ca²⁺ and/or Mg²⁺ ions.",
            "Step 2: These ions react with soap anions.",
            "Step 3: An insoluble substance called scum is formed."
          ],
          "why": "The insoluble calcium or magnesium soap removes soap from solution.",
          "sol": "Step 1: Hard water contains Ca²⁺ and/or Mg²⁺ ions.\nStep 2: These ions react with soap anions.\nStep 3: An insoluble substance called scum is formed.",
          "hint": "Focus on the core principle of Hard Water.",
          "subject": "chemistry",
          "chapter": "air_water_environment",
          "topic": "Hard Water",
          "conceptId": "chemistry_air_water_environment_hard_water",
          "skillId": "chemistry_air_water_environment",
