      "notes": "<h2>Acid Rain</h2>\n\n  <p>Acid rain is precipitation that is more acidic than normal because acidic substances formed in the atmosphere dissolve in rainwater.</p>\n\n  <h3>Main gases involved</h3>\n\n  <ul>\n    <li>Sulphur dioxide, SO₂</li>\n    <li>Nitrogen oxides, NOₓ</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h3>Effects of acid rain</h3>\n\n  <ul>\n    <li>Damages vegetation.</li>\n    <li>Acidifies lakes and rivers.</li>\n    <li>Can harm aquatic organisms.</li>\n    <li>Corrodes metals.</li>\n    <li>Can damage limestone and marble buildings.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h3>Control</h3>\n  <p>Reducing emissions of sulphur dioxide and nitrogen oxides reduces acid rain.</p>",
