          "why": "Calorific value provides a common measure of the energy content of fuels.",
          "sol": "Step 1: Calorific value measures energy released per unit mass.\nStep 2: Fuels can therefore be compared using the same mass basis.\nStep 3: A higher calorific value means more energy is released per unit mass.",
          "hint": "Focus on the core principle of Comparing Fuels.",
          "subject": "chemistry",
          "chapter": "chemical_energetics",
          "topic": "Comparing Fuels",
          "conceptId": "chemistry_chemical_energetics_comparing_fuels",
          "skillId": "chemistry_chemical_energetics",
          "subskillId": "chemistry_chemical_energetics_q2"
