          "q": "What is a simple cell?",
          "ans": "A simple cell is a device that converts chemical energy into electrical energy using chemical reactions between electrodes and an electrolyte.",
          "type": "text",
          "options": [],
          "steps": [
            "Step 1: A simple cell contains two electrodes and an electrolyte.",
            "Step 2: Chemical reactions occur at the electrodes.",
            "Step 3: These reactions cause electrons to flow through an external circuit.",
            "Step 4: The cell therefore converts chemical energy into electrical energy."
          ],
          "why": "Chemical reactions in the cell produce the electron flow that supplies electrical energy.",
